    {
      "claim": "Until the next unit wires the verb, a person or seat who runs landing prove on a tree the lane refuses by design sees a lane failure that invites a retry, not a refusal. The verb maps only the Busy error to a refusal; the new NoRepeat error is rendered as outcome failed with the words 'landing.prove.command could not run: this code failed its check and gets no other; give the goal that broke it back' and the retry hint 'tries again'.",
      "evidence": "metasystem/cmd/metasystem/intent_landing_prove.go lines 182 to 193: landingProveRefusal checks errors.As for *plain.Busy only and otherwise returns landingLaneFailure, whose result has Outcome failed and retry 'tries again'. The brief for this unit says 'No verb, no cmd wiring (the next unit)', and the design places cmd/metasystem in unit 3, so this is out of this unit's scope; it is recorded so unit 3 maps NoRepeat to a refusal whose next step is landing return. The bound itself holds: every retry is refused again, so no second check runs.",
