      "evidence": "Traced path: metasystem/internal/landing/plain/prove.go lines 146 to 156 (processRef returns empty when the probe fails), line 293 (Start stores it), lines 124 to 135 (the default alive returns false for an unparsable Process), lines 174 to 202 (checkState with attempt empty appends the stopped red and removes the record), then lines 363 to 399 (the detached Run finds no record, builds a fresh Running without Log and reads the stopped red through checkBound). Not reproduced; it needs the kernel probe of a freshly launched pid to fail, which the lane's week of use has not shown. Under R-124 the slice works and is safe without a fix; candidate for the later list (for example, Start treating an unreadable probe as alive until its attempt has a result, or the detached Run's first lock matching its attempt even when the record is gone).",
